WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:03.210
(sirens blasting)

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.960
(rhythmic music)

3
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:38.918 line:15%
(jazzy music)

4
00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:58.006
All righty, greetings everybody.

5
00:00:58.006 --> 00:01:01.022
Welcome to "Roll On" where curious Sir Adam Skolnick

6
00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:05.605
and I tap the non-alcoholic keg frothing with frivolity

7
00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:07.722
and matters of note,

8
00:01:07.722 --> 00:01:10.260
stories current that have captured our interest.

9
00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.010
We share a few products that we have enjoyed.

10
00:01:15.807 --> 00:01:17.914
We answer some listener questions, get up to no good,

11
00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:19.497
hopefully have a bit of fun while we're at it.

12
00:01:19.497 --> 00:01:22.869
But first, soon to inherit Sylvia Earl's crown,

13
00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:25.573
Lord of Malibu's underwater currents,

14
00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:28.874
his semi deepness himself, Mr. Adam Skolnick.

15
00:01:28.874 --> 00:01:30.457
How you doing?

16
00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.665
Semi deepness?

17
00:01:31.665 --> 00:01:33.123
Semi deepness.

18
00:01:33.123 --> 00:01:36.350
Well, you have not gone as deep as Sylvia.

19
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.183
No.

20
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:38.141
That's a fact.

21
00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:42.339
And to suggest I might inherit her crown anytime soon is,

22
00:01:42.339 --> 00:01:43.525
I don't know, it's borderline-

23
00:01:43.525 --> 00:01:44.858
It's preposterous.

24
00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:46.072
It is (laughs)

25
00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.030
I'm throwing it in your direction.

26
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.488
I appreciate it.

27
00:01:48.488 --> 00:01:50.486
You know, Rich, I can't complain.

28
00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:53.270
I am now the proud owner of life insurance.

29
00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.263
Wow.

30
00:01:54.263 --> 00:01:56.634
You are a middle aged Jewish man.

31
00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:59.594
Responsible, taking care of his family.

32
00:01:59.594 --> 00:02:03.698
Yeah, if I die tomorrow, April gets a million bucks.

33
00:02:03.698 --> 00:02:04.861
(Rich laughs)

34
00:02:04.861 --> 00:02:06.302
Well, it depends on how you die.

35
00:02:06.302 --> 00:02:07.385
Oh shit, wait.

36
00:02:07.385 --> 00:02:09.093
Oh no, I haven't signed it yet.

37
00:02:09.093 --> 00:02:11.301
So, after I sign it.

38
00:02:11.301 --> 00:02:14.094
If she kills you, she doesn't get it.

39
00:02:14.094 --> 00:02:16.092
Well, not if it's proven that way.

40
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:17.050
Right, okay.

41
00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.008
Do you have a plan?

42
00:02:18.008 --> 00:02:22.523
If I fake my own death, April gets a million bucks.

43
00:02:22.523 --> 00:02:24.100
They have to discover the body though.

44
00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.183
Oh, they need a body?

45
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:27.521
Yeah, there's, you know, caveats to all of that.

46
00:02:27.521 --> 00:02:28.604
Life insurance needs a body?

47
00:02:28.604 --> 00:02:29.562
I think so.

48
00:02:29.562 --> 00:02:30.395
Oh fuck.

49
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.853
Back to the drawing board.

50
00:02:32.853 --> 00:02:34.561
Rich, are you insured?

51
00:02:34.561 --> 00:02:35.394
I am.

52
00:02:35.394 --> 00:02:36.852
How well?

53
00:02:36.852 --> 00:02:38.310
I don't know.

54
00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.768
I should know.

55
00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:40.726
I think okay.

56
00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:41.975
You're pretty well insured, are ya?

57
00:02:41.975 --> 00:02:42.933
Okay.

58
00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:44.660
Well, mainly because if something happens to me,

59
00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:49.351
this whole thing stops and there's no business, right?

60
00:02:49.351 --> 00:02:51.404
That's the weird thing with podcasting.

61
00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:56.404
Like, I don't run a business that could continue without me.

62
00:02:56.512 --> 00:02:57.345
Right.

63
00:02:57.345 --> 00:02:58.932
And you're in the same situation.

64
00:02:58.932 --> 00:02:59.765
I am.

65
00:02:59.765 --> 00:03:02.811
I mean, look, listen, Ben and Jerry's has some nice benefits

66
00:03:02.811 --> 00:03:05.238
and I like the life insurance plan they got for me,

67
00:03:05.238 --> 00:03:06.185
but I needed to supplement.

68
00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.518
I needed to supplement.
Right, okay.

69
00:03:07.518 --> 00:03:10.253
How's it going over there scooping, scooping the dream?

70
00:03:10.253 --> 00:03:12.847
You know, I came down with scoop elbow.

71
00:03:12.847 --> 00:03:13.805
Have you ever heard of that?

72
00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:14.638
No.

73
00:03:14.638 --> 00:03:15.471
Scooper's elbow.

74
00:03:15.471 --> 00:03:16.304
Little tendonitis?

75
00:03:16.304 --> 00:03:18.364
Yeah, it's like one of the tendons in there.

76
00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.146
There's so many, I don't even, I can't.

77
00:03:20.146 --> 00:03:22.877
I used to memorize all my tendons but I stopped.

78
00:03:22.877 --> 00:03:24.560
Is that impacting your TikTok game?

79
00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.018
Oh dude, I don't do it for TikTok,

80
00:03:26.018 --> 00:03:28.101
I do it for the soul of scooping.

81
00:03:28.101 --> 00:03:32.052
All right, well, I wanted to say today's Monday.

82
00:03:32.052 --> 00:03:33.510
It's February 14th.

83
00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.619
That makes it Valentine's Day.

84
00:03:35.619 --> 00:03:37.043
Happy Valentine's Day, my friend.

85
00:03:37.043 --> 00:03:38.203
Happy Valentine's Day to you.

86
00:03:38.203 --> 00:03:42.370
And as much as I resent state-sponsored holidays

87
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.633
that mandate that we show affection for our loved ones,

88
00:03:46.633 --> 00:03:49.199
I could not resist the following.

89
00:03:49.199 --> 00:03:50.555
I got you a little something.

90
00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:51.388
What?

91
00:03:52.638 --> 00:03:53.721
This is terrible.

92
00:03:53.721 --> 00:03:56.054
Courtesy of the local CVS.

93
00:03:56.929 --> 00:03:58.512
You got me CVS roses?

94
00:03:58.512 --> 00:03:59.470
Yes.

95
00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.678
And CVS chocolates?

96
00:04:00.678 --> 00:04:05.001
Roses and candy for the love of my life.

97
00:04:05.001 --> 00:04:07.127
The bromance that knows no bounds.

98
00:04:07.127 --> 00:04:08.085
Thank you, bro.

99
00:04:08.085 --> 00:04:09.085
I got you...

100
00:04:11.043 --> 00:04:13.376
Your gift's in the mail.

101
00:04:13.376 --> 00:04:14.554
Your gift is in the mail.

102
00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.512
Yeah.

103
00:04:15.512 --> 00:04:16.470
There you go.

104
00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.522
I think I left the price on that too if you want to check.

105
00:04:19.522 --> 00:04:22.176
No, but there is a QR code.

106
00:04:22.176 --> 00:04:24.309
The Rainforest Alliance grew these.

107
00:04:24.309 --> 00:04:26.079
I think if you turn those flowers upside down,

108
00:04:26.079 --> 00:04:28.459
the petals might all fall off of all of them.

109
00:04:28.459 --> 00:04:30.678
(everyone laughs)

110
00:04:30.678 --> 00:04:32.386
There you go.

111
00:04:32.386 --> 00:04:34.094
You got me top quality flowers.

112
00:04:34.094 --> 00:04:35.389
Yeah, I did, I did.

113
00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:36.972
Nothing but the best.

114
00:04:36.972 --> 00:04:39.465
Were these left in a car overnight?

115
00:04:39.465 --> 00:04:40.423
No.

116
00:04:40.423 --> 00:04:42.338
I picked 'em up on the way over here this morning.

117
00:04:42.338 --> 00:04:44.466
Do you have a petal guy at the studio?

118
00:04:44.466 --> 00:04:45.424
A rose petal guy?
No, we could use one.

119
00:04:45.424 --> 00:04:49.680
We could use some flora and fauna here in the studio.

120
00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.138
I wish I had a gecko here.

121
00:04:51.138 --> 00:04:53.596
In addition to it being Valentine's Day,

122
00:04:53.596 --> 00:04:54.950
yesterday was the Super Bowl.

123
00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.908
How was your Super Bowl experience?

124
00:04:56.908 --> 00:04:58.491
You know, it was great.

125
00:04:58.491 --> 00:05:01.270
Thank God for DVR, for the geniuses behind DVR

126
00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.995
