150
00:05:51.523 --> 00:05:52.481
Did they not like that?

151
00:05:52.481 --> 00:05:54.940
No, this marks the, you know,

152
00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.306
the decline of human civilization,

153
00:05:57.306 --> 00:06:01.147
which is ironic because there was nothing new in that show.

154
00:06:01.147 --> 00:06:03.005
I mean, when did "8 Mile" come out?

155
00:06:03.005 --> 00:06:05.221
2006 or something like that.

156
00:06:05.221 --> 00:06:06.982
But what's the decline of human civilization

157
00:06:06.982 --> 00:06:07.815
that there's not,

158
00:06:07.815 --> 00:06:10.202
there's one show without a country music star?

159
00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:11.035
I don't know.

160
00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:11.868
I suppose.

161
00:06:12.743 --> 00:06:15.073
I liked Anderson .Paak as the drummer.

162
00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:16.908
Didn't see that coming.

163
00:06:16.908 --> 00:06:18.991
One of my top drummers.

164
00:06:18.991 --> 00:06:21.906
Ringo, Jason Camiolo, and Anderson .Paak.

165
00:06:21.906 --> 00:06:22.739
He's cool.

166
00:06:22.739 --> 00:06:24.197
His outfit was dope.

167
00:06:24.197 --> 00:06:25.155
Yeah, it was great.

168
00:06:25.155 --> 00:06:25.988
He was great.

169
00:06:25.988 --> 00:06:26.821
I don't know if people know,

170
00:06:26.821 --> 00:06:28.457
he's got some wonderful hip hop records.

171
00:06:28.457 --> 00:06:30.622
He's collaborating with Bruno Mars a lot now.

172
00:06:30.622 --> 00:06:33.266
He's got a band with Bruno Mars.

173
00:06:33.266 --> 00:06:36.243
But my favorite record of his is called "Malibu."

174
00:06:36.243 --> 00:06:38.298
And I don't know if you know that record.

175
00:06:38.298 --> 00:06:39.327
I don't know that record.

176
00:06:39.327 --> 00:06:40.160
It's fabulous.

177
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:40.993
Fabulous.

178
00:06:40.993 --> 00:06:41.826
Cool.

179
00:06:41.826 --> 00:06:43.966
I had the exciting good fortune

180
00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:46.090
of attending a Super Bowl party.

181
00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.048
You did?

182
00:06:47.048 --> 00:06:49.609
Yeah, Toby Morris, friend of the pod,

183
00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:53.156
invited me to join him at Frank Grillo's house.

184
00:06:53.156 --> 00:06:53.989
Okay.

185
00:06:53.989 --> 00:06:55.203
So, I went to a Super Bowl party.

186
00:06:55.203 --> 00:06:56.036
For people who don't know,

187
00:06:56.036 --> 00:06:58.826
Frank Grillo is sort of an action movie star.

188
00:06:58.826 --> 00:06:59.784
He's in like every movie.

189
00:06:59.784 --> 00:07:02.055
He's gotta be like one of the hardest working men

190
00:07:02.055 --> 00:07:03.263
in show business.

191
00:07:03.263 --> 00:07:04.221
I'd never met him before.

192
00:07:04.221 --> 00:07:05.554
He was delightful.

193
00:07:05.554 --> 00:07:09.861
And he's, I think he's 55, and just ridiculously fit.

194
00:07:09.861 --> 00:07:12.317
Maintains like 4% body fat year round.

195
00:07:12.317 --> 00:07:14.025
He's a boxer.

196
00:07:14.025 --> 00:07:15.483
Anyway, he was super kind.

197
00:07:15.483 --> 00:07:18.278
And we'll see if we can't get him on the podcast.

198
00:07:18.278 --> 00:07:19.245
Oh, cool!

199
00:07:19.245 --> 00:07:20.453
He seemed interested in coming on,

200
00:07:20.453 --> 00:07:21.661
so that might be fun.

201
00:07:21.661 --> 00:07:23.944
Was it weird to be at a Super Bowl party

202
00:07:23.944 --> 00:07:27.400
not really knowing that much about the players in the NFL?

203
00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.358
(Rich laughs)

204
00:07:29.358 --> 00:07:30.191
Slightly.

205
00:07:30.191 --> 00:07:31.679
I actually don't think I've watched the Super Bowl

206
00:07:31.679 --> 00:07:32.794
in like 10 years.

207
00:07:32.794 --> 00:07:33.627
I figured.

208
00:07:33.627 --> 00:07:34.908
And I was like, well, LA's in the Super Bowl.

209
00:07:34.908 --> 00:07:37.005
I enjoy the spectacle of the Super Bowl,

210
00:07:37.005 --> 00:07:38.829
