01:20:30.556 --> 01:20:33.181
for act three of this podcast.

2082
01:20:33.181 --> 01:20:34.139
Let's do it.

2083
01:20:34.139 --> 01:20:37.056
We're gonna start in New York City.

2084
01:20:38.393 --> 01:20:39.983
Yeah, baby.

2085
01:20:39.983 --> 01:20:40.941
Hey, Rich and Adam,

2086
01:20:40.941 --> 01:20:43.326
this is Brett calling from New York City.

2087
01:20:43.326 --> 01:20:45.167
Love the pod, love what you guys do.

2088
01:20:45.167 --> 01:20:46.375
Keep it coming.

2089
01:20:46.375 --> 01:20:48.290
My question is mostly for Rich,

2090
01:20:48.290 --> 01:20:50.370
although, Adam, would love for you to weigh in as well

2091
01:20:50.370 --> 01:20:52.446
if you feel it's relevant.

2092
01:20:52.446 --> 01:20:56.108
Rich, you have admitted to being prone towards negativity

2093
01:20:56.108 --> 01:20:57.623
and cynicism,

2094
01:20:57.623 --> 01:21:01.167
and I have to admit that I myself am inclined

2095
01:21:01.167 --> 01:21:03.389
in this direction as well.

2096
01:21:03.389 --> 01:21:05.027
And I'd love to hear from you

2097
01:21:05.027 --> 01:21:07.116
how you actively work against this

2098
01:21:07.116 --> 01:21:11.616
to show up in the world not negative, not pessimistic.

2099
01:21:12.572 --> 01:21:14.701
You've touched on this in many pods,

2100
01:21:14.701 --> 01:21:18.559
but today what I'm looking to hear is really pragmatic,

2101
01:21:18.559 --> 01:21:22.941
practical advice on how you work against this.

2102
01:21:22.941 --> 01:21:26.529
I think a lot of people out there would really benefit

2103
01:21:26.529 --> 01:21:30.363
from this type of advice with the world being what it is

2104
01:21:30.363 --> 01:21:34.664
with COVID, climate change, geopolitical issues.

2105
01:21:34.664 --> 01:21:36.825
We could all use this really practical advice.

2106
01:21:36.825 --> 01:21:39.226
Thanks so much guys, love you.

2107
01:21:39.226 --> 01:21:41.184
That's a great question, Bratt.

2108
01:21:41.184 --> 01:21:42.871
Is your name, is your name Bratt?

2109
01:21:42.871 --> 01:21:45.071
I think it's, maybe it's Brett.

2110
01:21:45.071 --> 01:21:46.279
Brett maybe.

2111
01:21:46.279 --> 01:21:47.737
I misheard it.

2112
01:21:47.737 --> 01:21:49.320
Brett from New York City.

2113
01:21:49.320 --> 01:21:51.653
I appreciate that question.

2114
01:21:51.653 --> 01:21:53.214
Yeah, you know, it's true

2115
01:21:53.214 --> 01:21:56.381
that I am not predisposed to optimism.

2116
01:21:57.924 --> 01:22:02.924
My default is not gratitude nor necessarily even positivity.

2117
01:22:03.780 --> 01:22:07.779
And I do find myself at times confounded by guests

2118
01:22:07.779 --> 01:22:09.832
that I've hosted over the years on the podcast

2119
01:22:09.832 --> 01:22:13.227
who seem to burst with unbridled optimism.

2120
01:22:13.227 --> 01:22:15.189
And sometimes I struggle with thinking like,

2121
01:22:15.189 --> 01:22:16.816
is that really even authentic?

2122
01:22:16.816 --> 01:22:18.981
Like, how is that person actually exuding

2123
01:22:18.981 --> 01:22:22.584
that level of positivity all the time?

2124
01:22:22.584 --> 01:22:23.542
It just happens.

2125
01:22:23.542 --> 01:22:25.797
I can't hold it inside, Rich!

2126
01:22:25.797 --> 01:22:27.154
I can't, it just comes,

2127
01:22:27.154 --> 01:22:27.987
it pours out of me.
I know, it's you.

2128
01:22:27.987 --> 01:22:30.404
I'm speaking directly to you.

2129
01:22:31.445 --> 01:22:35.057
And like, despite every counterpoint, you know,

2130
01:22:35.057 --> 01:22:36.760
I hurl in their direction,

2131
01:22:36.760 --> 01:22:40.475
nothing seems capable of derailing that positivity.

2132
01:22:40.475 --> 01:22:41.558
And I admire that.

2133
01:22:41.558 --> 01:22:43.217
You know, that's a sensibility

2134
01:22:43.217 --> 01:22:46.407
that I wish I could inhabit more and better,

2135
01:22:46.407 --> 01:22:50.107
but which despite, you know, fleeting flirtations,

2136
01:22:50.107 --> 01:22:53.020
I do not consistently exude myself,

2137
01:22:53.020 --> 01:22:54.770
so I feel you, Brett.

2138
01:22:55.728 --> 01:22:58.423
For example, like just the other day, like two days ago,

2139
01:22:58.423 --> 01:23:01.994
I woke up feeling not great, I slept poorly,

2140
01:23:01.994 --> 01:23:04.422
and I was just like a disaster all day.

2141
01:23:04.422 --> 01:23:06.005
I was dark, I was moody.

2142
01:23:06.005 --> 01:23:07.088
I felt angry.

2143
01:23:07.088 --> 01:23:09.667
I felt unfit to be around other people.

2144
01:23:09.667 --> 01:23:13.658
And I had like no energy or enthusiasm for anything.

2145
01:23:13.658 --> 01:23:15.940
And this is like a darkness that befalls on me

2146
01:23:15.940 --> 01:23:17.148
from time to time.

2147
01:23:17.148 --> 01:23:18.808
In this case, it was directly related

2148
01:23:18.808 --> 01:23:20.808
to not waking up rested.

2149
01:23:22.641 --> 01:23:25.516
And so, I have over the years developed a couple strategies

2150
01:23:25.516 --> 01:23:29.201
for combating this and dealing with this.

2151
01:23:29.201 --> 01:23:33.635
And, you know, the first thing is to just accept it.

2152
01:23:33.635 --> 01:23:37.061
You know, like to kind of be angry that you're feeling

2153
01:23:37.061 --> 01:23:39.558
that way is only making it worse

2154
01:23:39.558 --> 01:23:41.806
and enhances the level of suffering

2155
01:23:41.806 --> 01:23:43.301
that you're experiencing.

2156
01:23:43.301 --> 01:23:45.961
I also think it's important to always remind myself

2157
01:23:45.961 --> 01:23:50.628
that like cynicism is kind of a lazy reaction to things.

2158
01:23:51.715 --> 01:23:54.004
I think it takes a lot more gumption

2159
01:23:54.004 --> 01:23:58.964
and courage to be optimistic and have a positive outlook.

2160
01:23:58.964 --> 01:24:01.422
So, I remind myself of that.

2161
01:24:01.422 --> 01:24:03.864
When I do feel that way, I try not to dwell on it

2162
01:24:03.864 --> 01:24:05.842
or beat myself up for it

2163
01:24:05.842 --> 01:24:07.955
again 'cause that creates kind of a vicious cycle

2164
01:24:07.955 --> 01:24:10.728
that seems to perpetuate it and make it worse.

2165
01:24:10.728 --> 01:24:14.267
And then I try to engage in really simple activities

2166
01:24:14.267 --> 01:24:15.475
to help shift it.

2167
01:24:15.475 --> 01:24:19.016
Like, go for a walk or even a 10 minute meditation

2168
01:24:19.016 --> 01:24:21.330
or, you know what, I'm feeling off,

2169
01:24:21.330 --> 01:24:23.598
like maybe I should go to an AA meeting.

2170
01:24:23.598 --> 01:24:26.195
And, you know, take those actions

2171
01:24:26.195 --> 01:24:28.524
because it's only truly through actions

2172
01:24:28.524 --> 01:24:30.721
that you can kind of shift that perspective.

2173
01:24:30.721 --> 01:24:33.520
And then beyond that, like trying to remind myself

2174
01:24:33.520 --> 01:24:36.244
that it's okay to feel however you feel.

2175
01:24:36.244 --> 01:24:39.175
Like, being okay with yourself.

2176
01:24:39.175 --> 01:24:41.675
And then from there, you know,

2177
01:24:43.212 --> 01:24:44.390
I try to engage in practices

2178
01:24:44.390 --> 01:24:48.500
that lead to or cultivate more optimism, positivity,

2179
01:24:48.500 --> 01:24:50.193
and gratitude in my life.

2180
01:24:50.193 --> 01:24:52.195
All of which I've talked about many times

2181
01:24:52.195 --> 01:24:53.756
at length on the podcast.

2182
01:24:53.756 --> 01:24:56.227
And I think for the most part are things

2183
01:24:56.227 --> 01:24:58.790
that are pretty self evident and not complicated.

2184
01:24:58.790 --> 01:25:02.452
And they all trace back to this idea of mood follows action,

2185
01:25:02.452 --> 01:25:03.954
this mantra, right?

2186
01:25:03.954 --> 01:25:07.128
If you wanna shift your mental or emotional disposition,

2187
01:25:07.128 --> 01:25:09.815
you have to do something to accomplish that.

2188
01:25:09.815 --> 01:25:12.008
So, are you getting enough sleep?

2189
01:25:12.008 --> 01:25:14.218
Are you exercising on the daily?

2190
01:25:14.218 --> 01:25:15.342
Are you connecting with nature?

2191
01:25:15.342 --> 01:25:17.529
Are you connecting with other people?

2192
01:25:17.529 --> 01:25:21.424
Are you of service to somebody less fortunate like often?

2193
01:25:21.424 --> 01:25:24.076
And this is, you know, completely a 12 step thing.

2194
01:25:24.076 --> 01:25:25.577
Like, if you feel off

2195
01:25:25.577 --> 01:25:30.389
or you're grinding on your own, you know, self-obsession,

2196
01:25:30.389 --> 01:25:32.628
like pick up the phone and call a friend

2197
01:25:32.628 --> 01:25:33.971
who's going through a hard time.

2198
01:25:33.971 --> 01:25:36.267
It doesn't have to be some huge grand gesture,

2199
01:25:36.267 --> 01:25:38.079
but anything you can do to kind of get

2200
01:25:38.079 --> 01:25:40.454
out of your own self-obsession seems

2201
01:25:40.454 --> 01:25:44.923
to ameliorate those kind of negative emotions.

2202
01:25:44.923 --> 01:25:47.649
And then beyond that, you know, again, simple stuff.

2203
01:25:47.649 --> 01:25:50.140
Meditation, mindfulness practices,

2204
01:25:50.140 --> 01:25:54.140
a gratitude list which helps shift the narrative

2205
01:25:56.247 --> 01:26:00.399
and helps you identify or kind of appreciate

2206
01:26:00.399 --> 01:26:02.899
that there are a lot of good things in your life

2207
01:26:02.899 --> 01:26:05.454
and maybe, you know, in my case, my life is crazy good.

2208
01:26:05.454 --> 01:26:06.456
I lose sight of that

2209
01:26:06.456 --> 01:26:10.373
unless I intentionally practice contrary action

2210
01:26:11.463 --> 01:26:12.921
and behavior.

2211
01:26:12.921 --> 01:26:16.231
So, stop dwelling on the enormity of problems

2212
01:26:16.231 --> 01:26:17.641
that you're powerless to solve.

2213
01:26:17.641 --> 01:26:18.982
Like, you talked about climate change,

2214
01:26:18.982 --> 01:26:20.445
like these existential things.

2215
01:26:20.445 --> 01:26:23.198
Like, you can walk around with a cloud over your head,

2216
01:26:23.198 --> 01:26:25.340
and it will paralyze you.

2217
01:26:25.340 --> 01:26:29.612
So, try to get out of that kind of dooms day scrolling

2218
01:26:29.612 --> 01:26:32.904
or dooms day thinking and just focus on

2219
01:26:32.904 --> 01:26:35.815
and execute the small things that you can actually do

2220
01:26:35.815 --> 01:26:39.016
on the daily and then do them.

2221
01:26:39.016 --> 01:26:40.004
And here's the thing.

2222
01:26:40.004 --> 01:26:43.081
And again, this is another like 12 step thing.

2223
01:26:43.081 --> 01:26:44.414
These solutions,

2224
01:26:44.414 --> 01:26:47.308
it's like I'm sure Brett already knows all of this, right?

2225
01:26:47.308 --> 01:26:49.303
Sometimes we need to be reminded of them

2226
01:26:49.303 --> 01:26:53.606
because inherently as humans like we're annoyed

2227
01:26:53.606 --> 01:26:56.121
that the solution or the answer

2228
01:26:56.121 --> 01:26:58.481
again goes back to these basic things.

2229
01:26:58.481 --> 01:27:00.099
We want it to be more complicated.

2230
01:27:00.099 --> 01:27:02.182
Or what's the better solution?

2231
01:27:02.182 --> 01:27:03.652
Or what's the latest in science

2232
01:27:03.652 --> 01:27:05.365
that can solve this problem for me?

2233
01:27:05.365 --> 01:27:06.591
Where's the advanced course?

2234
01:27:06.591 --> 01:27:09.219
How can I get, you know, beyond the velvet rope,

2235
01:27:09.219 --> 01:27:10.962
and you can tell me the new thing

2236
01:27:10.962 --> 01:27:13.293
that I can do to deal with this stuff.

2237
01:27:13.293 --> 01:27:16.001
But there is no magic bullet.

2238
01:27:16.001 --> 01:27:17.959
It's the same old shit.

2239
01:27:17.959 --> 01:27:20.391
And no matter how much you practice meditation

2240
01:27:20.391 --> 01:27:21.776
or no matter, you know,

2241
01:27:21.776 --> 01:27:23.894
how many times you get a good night's sleep,

2242
01:27:23.894 --> 01:27:25.864
like it doesn't carry into the next day.

2243
01:27:25.864 --> 01:27:29.125
These are things you have to do consistently

2244
01:27:29.125 --> 01:27:31.208
every single day if you're in that place

2245
01:27:31.208 --> 01:27:33.041
if you want to emerge out of it.

2246
01:27:33.041 --> 01:27:36.373
It's just doing these things over and over again,

2247
01:27:36.373 --> 01:27:37.552
rinse and repeat.

2248
01:27:37.552 --> 01:27:39.129
And that's not to say, you know,

2249
01:27:39.129 --> 01:27:42.054
sometimes people need some exogenous help.

2250
01:27:42.054 --> 01:27:45.816
Like, if you have a true case of depression,

2251
01:27:45.816 --> 01:27:48.737
clinical depression, or some other kind of mental condition,

2252
01:27:48.737 --> 01:27:51.200
then you should seek help for that.

2253
01:27:51.200 --> 01:27:53.842
Whether that's therapeutic talk therapy,

2254
01:27:53.842 --> 01:27:56.085
which is another thing that, you know, I think is good

2255
01:27:56.085 --> 01:27:58.423
and what I've been practicing for many years,

2256
01:27:58.423 --> 01:28:01.640
or some kind of, you know, outside help in that vein.

2257
01:28:01.640 --> 01:28:04.044
But that's the best answer that I can give you.

2258
01:28:04.044 --> 01:28:05.800
And I hope that's helpful.

2259
01:28:05.800 --> 01:28:07.383
That was a fantastic answer.

2260
01:28:07.383 --> 01:28:09.091
She wanted to hear from you too.

2261
01:28:09.091 --> 01:28:10.969
If I felt it was applicable.

2262
01:28:10.969 --> 01:28:15.648
I think she senses that I have an internal buoyancy control,

2263
01:28:15.648 --> 01:28:18.605
which I don't get into like the,

2264
01:28:18.605 --> 01:28:22.170
I don't wake up with like the dark drearies.

2265
01:28:22.170 --> 01:28:25.249
But you have a comedic cynicism to you.

2266
01:28:25.249 --> 01:28:28.833
Oh, I have a deeply embedded like global cynicism

2267
01:28:28.833 --> 01:28:29.916
within me.

2268
01:28:29.916 --> 01:28:31.124
I do, I am concern-

2269
01:28:31.124 --> 01:28:34.916
But rather than combat it, you cultivate it.

2270
01:28:34.916 --> 01:28:35.999
It's part of my persona.

2271
01:28:35.999 --> 01:28:37.082
And then you deploy that.

2272
01:28:37.082 --> 01:28:38.290
But like, it doesn't,

2273
01:28:38.290 --> 01:28:39.373
what I'm saying is it doesn't,

2274
01:28:39.373 --> 01:28:41.782
I don't wake up like feeling that.

2275
01:28:41.782 --> 01:28:43.139
You know what gets me?

2276
01:28:43.139 --> 01:28:44.518
Is when I have a lot to do

2277
01:28:44.518 --> 01:28:46.222
and I don't feel like I have enough time.

2278
01:28:46.222 --> 01:28:49.245
And like the big stuff, like the real crises,

2279
01:28:49.245 --> 01:28:50.703
I'm actually good,

2280
01:28:50.703 --> 01:28:52.985
I'm actually able to deal with quite well.

2281
01:28:52.985 --> 01:28:55.476
It's the stuff that is actually not a crisis

2282
01:28:55.476 --> 01:28:57.645
that I make into a bigger deal than it is,

2283
01:28:57.645 --> 01:28:58.913
and it drives me nuts.

2284
01:28:58.913 --> 01:29:01.648
So, I'm like kind of the opposite, if that makes sense.

2285
01:29:01.648 --> 01:29:03.865
Like, I don't get caught up in like the stuff you-

2286
01:29:03.865 --> 01:29:04.948
It's not climate change.

2287
01:29:04.948 --> 01:29:07.936
It's like why is there a scuff on my shoe?

2288
01:29:07.936 --> 01:29:10.343
It's like there's so many deadlines

2289
01:29:10.343 --> 01:29:11.614
and there's other things I wanna do,

2290
01:29:11.614 --> 01:29:12.523
and you know what I mean?

2291
01:29:12.523 --> 01:29:14.151
Like, and when am I gonna,

2292
01:29:14.151 --> 01:29:17.086
it's looking for the next thing is my big dilemma.

2293
01:29:17.086 --> 01:29:20.034
But that said, I certainly have really bad days.

2294
01:29:20.034 --> 01:29:21.767
And sometimes I am the asshole,

2295
01:29:21.767 --> 01:29:24.649
and you always don't wanna be the asshole in the world,

2296
01:29:24.649 --> 01:29:25.982
but sometimes you are.

2297
01:29:25.982 --> 01:29:30.690
And what I usually, if I'm not doing daily yoga

2298
01:29:30.690 --> 01:29:34.080
in the morning or exercising first thing in the morning,

2299
01:29:34.080 --> 01:29:36.709
I'm much more susceptible to that.

2300
01:29:36.709 --> 01:29:40.313
So, for me, the big, the big thing is movement.

2301
01:29:40.313 --> 01:29:43.993
And if I do that and I can usually keep my mind right.

2302
01:29:43.993 --> 01:29:46.524
Yeah, you can't be the person you want to be in the world

2303
01:29:46.524 --> 01:29:48.974
if you're not exercising some basic self care.

2304
01:29:48.974 --> 01:29:50.182
Right.

2305
01:29:50.182 --> 01:29:51.265
And then I like I do,

2306
01:29:51.265 --> 01:29:53.537
it is important to me to stay in that connection

2307
01:29:53.537 --> 01:29:54.745
and all of that.

2308
01:29:54.745 --> 01:29:57.523
But like I said, I am cynical in a lot of ways.

2309
01:29:57.523 --> 01:30:01.438
I just don't wake up with the drearies too often.

2310
01:30:01.438 --> 01:30:04.240
All right, well, let's go to Bill from Crusted Butte.

2311
01:30:04.240 --> 01:30:06.367
Hey, Rich and Adam,

2312
01:30:06.367 --> 01:30:08.437
thank you so much for what you guys do.

2313
01:30:08.437 --> 01:30:11.334
This is Bill Wolfson out of Crested Butte, Colorado.

2314
01:30:11.334 --> 01:30:15.667
I am calling to ask a question regarding discipline.

2315
01:30:19.220 --> 01:30:23.837
I have the goals and aspirations of being a vegan,

2316
01:30:23.837 --> 01:30:28.254
socially, physically, and morally, I guess you'd say.

2317
01:30:29.379 --> 01:30:31.962
And I am lacking some fortitude

2318
01:30:33.324 --> 01:30:36.657
or some ability to really stick with it,

2319
01:30:37.613 --> 01:30:41.000
either based on social influences, my own discipline,

2320
01:30:41.000 --> 01:30:42.833
or just inconsistency.

2321
01:30:44.251 --> 01:30:47.150
I've gotten past beating myself up for it,

2322
01:30:47.150 --> 01:30:50.098
but that was also a struggle for a while.

2323
01:30:50.098 --> 01:30:53.008
And now I'm just wondering if you have any tips or tricks

2324
01:30:53.008 --> 01:30:55.469
for some of us people that struggle with this.

2325
01:30:55.469 --> 01:30:58.150
I'm guessing it's a relatively common occurrence

2326
01:30:58.150 --> 01:31:02.067
for a lot of people who love what you guys do

2327
01:31:02.067 --> 01:31:03.525
and how you do it,

2328
01:31:03.525 --> 01:31:06.525
but they're not 100% integrated

2329
01:31:07.533 --> 01:31:10.390
on how we are doing it in our own lives.

2330
01:31:10.390 --> 01:31:11.598
Thank you so much.

2331
01:31:11.598 --> 01:31:14.992
I hope you can shed some light on this,

2332
01:31:14.992 --> 01:31:18.492
and peace, plants, and namaste to you all.

2333
01:31:19.384 --> 01:31:20.217
Thanks Bill.

2334
01:31:20.217 --> 01:31:21.733
I think that's a great question.

2335
01:31:21.733 --> 01:31:24.772
It is a common issue that I think we all confront

2336
01:31:24.772 --> 01:31:25.605
in our own ways.

2337
01:31:25.605 --> 01:31:29.686
I mean, you use the example of striving to go vegan,

2338
01:31:29.686 --> 01:31:31.619
but this quandary I think applies

2339
01:31:31.619 --> 01:31:33.344
to any type of habit change.

2340
01:31:33.344 --> 01:31:35.674
So, the question first is

2341
01:31:35.674 --> 01:31:37.830
why is letting go of bad habits so hard

2342
01:31:37.830 --> 01:31:41.248
and why is creating better habits equally hard

2343
01:31:41.248 --> 01:31:42.956
if not harder?

2344
01:31:42.956 --> 01:31:46.535
Many people smarter than me have tackled this terrain.

2345
01:31:46.535 --> 01:31:49.430
So, I would start with the wisdom of James Clear

2346
01:31:49.430 --> 01:31:51.288
in his book "Atomic Habits."

2347
01:31:51.288 --> 01:31:54.157
We did a podcast together that was very popular.

2348
01:31:54.157 --> 01:31:58.191
It was a couple years ago, October, 2018, episode 401.

2349
01:31:58.191 --> 01:32:00.817
So, I would check that out if you haven't already.

2350
01:32:00.817 --> 01:32:03.484
But I think a lot of this begins

2351
01:32:04.567 --> 01:32:07.706
with identifying your values.

2352
01:32:07.706 --> 01:32:10.913
And what I mean by that is first being clear

2353
01:32:10.913 --> 01:32:14.685
on who you are now and who you aspire to be.

2354
01:32:14.685 --> 01:32:18.887
So, the values that you desire to inhabit,

2355
01:32:18.887 --> 01:32:21.686
like what does that look like for you?

2356
01:32:21.686 --> 01:32:23.935
And then getting really clear on the dissonance

2357
01:32:23.935 --> 01:32:24.768
between the two,

2358
01:32:24.768 --> 01:32:27.503
the person you are now and the person you aspire to be.

2359
01:32:27.503 --> 01:32:30.420
And I think that in between zone...

2360
01:32:32.590 --> 01:32:33.673
Within that in between zone,

2361
01:32:33.673 --> 01:32:37.094
there is a dissonance that creates a psychic toll

2362
01:32:37.094 --> 01:32:42.094
that I believe is a barrier to really feeling comfortable

2363
01:32:42.529 --> 01:32:46.466
in your own skin and living as authentically as you can.

2364
01:32:46.466 --> 01:32:48.430
So, the less dissonance between those two,

2365
01:32:48.430 --> 01:32:51.140
the more fully embodied and empowered you're going to feel

2366
01:32:51.140 --> 01:32:52.223
and become.

2367
01:32:52.223 --> 01:32:53.293
So, that's the goal, right?

2368
01:32:53.293 --> 01:32:54.251
How do we get there?

2369
01:32:54.251 --> 01:32:57.463
Well, to close that gap and eat away at that dissonance,

2370
01:32:57.463 --> 01:33:00.341
you need to know the end game first,

2371
01:33:00.341 --> 01:33:01.544
the person you aspire to be.

2372
01:33:01.544 --> 01:33:03.371
So again, back to that clarity.

2373
01:33:03.371 --> 01:33:05.197
And then you need to backtrack from there

2374
01:33:05.197 --> 01:33:08.862
and identify the steps that are going to get you there.

2375
01:33:08.862 --> 01:33:09.820
So, there's a goal,

2376
01:33:09.820 --> 01:33:12.278
and then there's the stepping stones

2377
01:33:12.278 --> 01:33:14.069
towards achieving that goal.

2378
01:33:14.069 --> 01:33:17.894
And I think as you begin to identify those steps

2379
01:33:17.894 --> 01:33:20.208
and begin to take them,

2380
01:33:20.208 --> 01:33:23.390
a perspective that I think is helpful is to look at it

2381
01:33:23.390 --> 01:33:25.959
through the lens of forming new habits

2382
01:33:25.959 --> 01:33:28.353
rather than letting go of bad habits.

2383
01:33:28.353 --> 01:33:30.780
So, rather than dwell on the bad habits,

2384
01:33:30.780 --> 01:33:33.922
which tend to lead you to beating yourself up,

2385
01:33:33.922 --> 01:33:35.130
sort of let go of that

2386
01:33:35.130 --> 01:33:38.410
or put it in the back recesses of your mind

2387
01:33:38.410 --> 01:33:40.957
and focus on the new habits that you're trying to build.

2388
01:33:40.957 --> 01:33:44.117
These new steps, these new stepping stones are going

2389
01:33:44.117 --> 01:33:47.953
to be the fabric upon which you build these new habits

2390
01:33:47.953 --> 01:33:49.783
until they are fully ingrained.

2391
01:33:49.783 --> 01:33:52.970
And the way that you do that is you identify

2392
01:33:52.970 --> 01:33:55.431
and start with really small doable things

2393
01:33:55.431 --> 01:33:57.299
that you can begin doing right away.

2394
01:33:57.299 --> 01:33:59.938
Things that are just a little bit out of your comfort zone

2395
01:33:59.938 --> 01:34:01.385
but not too much out.

2396
01:34:01.385 --> 01:34:03.362
Like, there shouldn't be too much of a stretch.

2397
01:34:03.362 --> 01:34:06.411
And then you start knocking them down, like doing them.

2398
01:34:06.411 --> 01:34:08.494
And that creates momentum.

2399
01:34:08.494 --> 01:34:10.327
And with that momentum,

2400
01:34:10.327 --> 01:34:12.798
you'll find yourself more emotionally engaged

2401
01:34:12.798 --> 01:34:14.506
with the journey itself.

2402
01:34:14.506 --> 01:34:18.097
And then it's about just continuing to keep the pressure on

2403
01:34:18.097 --> 01:34:20.381
and increasing the degree of difficulty

2404
01:34:20.381 --> 01:34:24.423
of those little doable steps as you kind of progress.

2405
01:34:24.423 --> 01:34:26.291
And I think when you do this,

2406
01:34:26.291 --> 01:34:28.342
as you're building these new habits,

2407
01:34:28.342 --> 01:34:31.889
often what happens is it will crowd out the bad habits

2408
01:34:31.889 --> 01:34:33.830
and they will fall away without effort.

2409
01:34:33.830 --> 01:34:36.911
So, without even focusing on letting go of these bad habits,

2410
01:34:36.911 --> 01:34:39.894
the new habits will create so much space

2411
01:34:39.894 --> 01:34:41.409
that there isn't really any room

2412
01:34:41.409 --> 01:34:42.666
for those bad habits anymore.

2413
01:34:42.666 --> 01:34:45.810
And they will kind of evaporate

2414
01:34:45.810 --> 01:34:47.726
without having to put a lot of, you know,

2415
01:34:47.726 --> 01:34:49.726
mental effort into them.

2416
01:34:50.934 --> 01:34:55.684
I think that it's also important to create an environment

2417
01:34:57.378 --> 01:35:01.890
that's conducive to making those healthy changes

2418
01:35:01.890 --> 01:35:06.057
and leading you to take those little, little steps

2419
01:35:07.013 --> 01:35:08.096
along the way.

2420
01:35:08.096 --> 01:35:10.427
So, in the context of this vegan example,

2421
01:35:10.427 --> 01:35:12.723
it's like get rid of the foods in your house

2422
01:35:12.723 --> 01:35:13.873
that aren't on the program,

2423
01:35:13.873 --> 01:35:17.803
and that way you make it additionally more difficult

2424
01:35:17.803 --> 01:35:21.033
for you to veer off the path that you're, you know,

2425
01:35:21.033 --> 01:35:22.491
trying to walk.

2426
01:35:22.491 --> 01:35:26.095
And I think also it's important to be patient

2427
01:35:26.095 --> 01:35:27.899
and gentle with yourself.

2428
01:35:27.899 --> 01:35:29.357
This is not a linear thing.

2429
01:35:29.357 --> 01:35:30.940
It's not about perfection.

2430
01:35:30.940 --> 01:35:32.535
If you slip up or make a mistake,

2431
01:35:32.535 --> 01:35:35.341
it's not about beating yourself up or abandoning it.

2432
01:35:35.341 --> 01:35:39.325
It's about doing a forensic evaluation of why you mistepped

2433
01:35:39.325 --> 01:35:41.908
and trying to understand what led you to that choice

2434
01:35:41.908 --> 01:35:43.116
and then closing that gap,

2435
01:35:43.116 --> 01:35:46.329
so that next time you're not in that position again.

2436
01:35:46.329 --> 01:35:49.433
Like, "Oh, I was feeling tired,"

2437
01:35:49.433 --> 01:35:51.672
or, "I just had an argument with my partner

2438
01:35:51.672 --> 01:35:53.753
"and suddenly I found myself eating this thing

2439
01:35:53.753 --> 01:35:55.086
"I promised myself I wouldn't."

2440
01:35:55.086 --> 01:35:57.654
Like, you know, first of all, get the thing out of the house

2441
01:35:57.654 --> 01:35:58.737
and then understand like,

2442
01:35:58.737 --> 01:36:01.364
"Oh, wow, I guess like I veer off the path

2443
01:36:01.364 --> 01:36:03.447
"when I'm in this emotional state."

2444
01:36:03.447 --> 01:36:07.010
Like, all of those things I think are building

2445
01:36:07.010 --> 01:36:10.265
your self knowledge and self understanding

2446
01:36:10.265 --> 01:36:11.888
about why you make the choices that you make,

2447
01:36:11.888 --> 01:36:13.721
and those turn out to be very helpful.

2448
01:36:13.721 --> 01:36:15.554
Back to the patience thing.

2449
01:36:15.554 --> 01:36:17.408
Progress is generally microscopic.

2450
01:36:17.408 --> 01:36:20.422
Often a other people are able to identify changes

2451
01:36:20.422 --> 01:36:23.482
that you've made in yourself before you're even able to.

2452
01:36:23.482 --> 01:36:25.770
So, if you're not seeing it in yourself

2453
01:36:25.770 --> 01:36:27.590
or you feel like you're not making any progress,

2454
01:36:27.590 --> 01:36:30.298
that's not necessarily a pragmatic

2455
01:36:30.298 --> 01:36:32.547
or reliable indicator of where you are.

2456
01:36:32.547 --> 01:36:36.672
Just keep doing the thing, keep like trotting the path,

2457
01:36:36.672 --> 01:36:38.363
and build on that momentum.

2458
01:36:38.363 --> 01:36:41.697
And if need be, leverage external accountability,

2459
01:36:41.697 --> 01:36:43.582
both positive and negative.

2460
01:36:43.582 --> 01:36:44.921
Like, bring people into your life

2461
01:36:44.921 --> 01:36:45.879
to whom you're accountable.

2462
01:36:45.879 --> 01:36:48.307
Like, people that know you're trying to do this hard thing

2463
01:36:48.307 --> 01:36:49.832
that you're checking in with

2464
01:36:49.832 --> 01:36:53.814
who are aware of whether you're, you know,

2465
01:36:53.814 --> 01:36:55.397
doing it properly or not.

2466
01:36:55.397 --> 01:36:57.195
And they can say, "Hey, what's up?

2467
01:36:57.195 --> 01:36:59.117
"You said you were gonna go to the gym at this time.

2468
01:36:59.117 --> 01:37:00.454
"You didn't show up," or whatever.

2469
01:37:00.454 --> 01:37:03.145
Like, the more you can kind of build in those measures,

2470
01:37:03.145 --> 01:37:07.812
the more likely you are to, you know, remain on that path.

2471
01:37:07.812 --> 01:37:12.661
And I think it's also important because these, you know,

2472
01:37:12.661 --> 01:37:15.387
sometimes, like you wanna make a big change in your life.

2473
01:37:15.387 --> 01:37:17.651
Like, I want to go vegan and let go of these animal products

2474
01:37:17.651 --> 01:37:19.339
that I have been eating my whole life.

2475
01:37:19.339 --> 01:37:23.753
Like, that's a large thing that you're endeavoring to do,

2476
01:37:23.753 --> 01:37:24.586
right?

2477
01:37:24.586 --> 01:37:28.114
So, the best way is to break it down into tiny little things

2478
01:37:28.114 --> 01:37:29.811
and master one thing at a time.

2479
01:37:29.811 --> 01:37:31.543
So, an example that I always like to give

2480
01:37:31.543 --> 01:37:33.751
in the vegan context is, you know,

2481
01:37:33.751 --> 01:37:36.906
maybe swap out dairy milk for plant milk,

2482
01:37:36.906 --> 01:37:39.747
and put that in your coffee or tea in the morning,

2483
01:37:39.747 --> 01:37:42.177
or put that on your cereal, or however you use milk.

2484
01:37:42.177 --> 01:37:45.189
And just do that for a period of, I don't know,

2485
01:37:45.189 --> 01:37:46.948
six weeks or eight weeks.

2486
01:37:46.948 --> 01:37:49.554
And what you'll find is suddenly you won't think twice

2487
01:37:49.554 --> 01:37:50.387
about it.

2488
01:37:50.387 --> 01:37:52.330
It's just the default choice that you make.

2489
01:37:52.330 --> 01:37:55.353
And then you can move on to another category,

2490
01:37:55.353 --> 01:37:57.239
and you kind of knock those, you know,

2491
01:37:57.239 --> 01:37:58.992
bowling pins down one at a time.

2492
01:37:58.992 --> 01:38:02.541
And I think, you know, when you do it that way,

2493
01:38:02.541 --> 01:38:03.374
then you're kind of,

2494
01:38:03.374 --> 01:38:05.096
you can celebrate these little successes too.

2495
01:38:05.096 --> 01:38:08.177
And the more little successes that you can celebrate,

2496
01:38:08.177 --> 01:38:09.956
then the better you feel about the progress

2497
01:38:09.956 --> 01:38:11.473
that you're making

2498
01:38:11.473 --> 01:38:14.037
and the more emotionally invested you are in, you know,

2499
01:38:14.037 --> 01:38:18.320
the long term plan of what you're trying to accomplish.

2500
01:38:18.320 --> 01:38:21.686
Final thing I would say is it's important

2501
01:38:21.686 --> 01:38:24.995
to look inward within yourself

2502
01:38:24.995 --> 01:38:28.216
and kind of deconstruct your own psychological framework

2503
01:38:28.216 --> 01:38:31.043
because you said in your question

2504
01:38:31.043 --> 01:38:33.965
that your resolve often fails

2505
01:38:33.965 --> 01:38:35.192
in the face of social influence.

2506
01:38:35.192 --> 01:38:36.617
So like why is that the case?

2507
01:38:36.617 --> 01:38:40.096
And what does it say about how you feel about yourself

2508
01:38:40.096 --> 01:38:43.354
and your ability to set healthy boundaries?

2509
01:38:43.354 --> 01:38:45.948
Like, the idea that you would cave who you wanna be

2510
01:38:45.948 --> 01:38:48.113
because someone might be uncomfortable with it,

2511
01:38:48.113 --> 01:38:53.113
that tells me that you lack a certain level of esteem

2512
01:38:53.163 --> 01:38:54.746
to stand in your own truth,

2513
01:38:54.746 --> 01:38:56.997
the fact you would change your habits

2514
01:38:56.997 --> 01:38:59.907
because you're in a certain social setting

2515
01:38:59.907 --> 01:39:02.072
where people might have a certain opinion

2516
01:39:02.072 --> 01:39:04.655
about what you're doing.

2517
01:39:04.655 --> 01:39:07.592
But each act that you take to align your behavior

2518
01:39:07.592 --> 01:39:10.999
with this value set is like a building block

2519
01:39:10.999 --> 01:39:13.748
in your fortress of self-esteem.

2520
01:39:13.748 --> 01:39:16.551
So, what it will do over time is allow yourself

2521
01:39:16.551 --> 01:39:17.884
to be who you are.

2522
01:39:17.884 --> 01:39:21.779
And I think you'll find as I have that those people

2523
01:39:21.779 --> 01:39:24.507
that you're so afraid are judging you,

2524
01:39:24.507 --> 01:39:27.283
not only don't really give a shit

2525
01:39:27.283 --> 01:39:28.698
because everyone is self-absorbed

2526
01:39:28.698 --> 01:39:30.906
and they're just thinking about themselves,

2527
01:39:30.906 --> 01:39:35.414
but that in fact, they will actually respect you more for,

2528
01:39:35.414 --> 01:39:38.877
you know, what I would consider to be an esteemable act.

2529
01:39:38.877 --> 01:39:40.551
Like, "Hey, I don't do that anymore, I'm doing this,"

2530
01:39:40.551 --> 01:39:41.759
it has nothing to do with other people.

2531
01:39:41.759 --> 01:39:44.952
This is about your relationship with you and you.

2532
01:39:44.952 --> 01:39:46.850
And I think getting clarity on that

2533
01:39:46.850 --> 01:39:50.108
and having the gumption or the courage to, you know,

2534
01:39:50.108 --> 01:39:52.945
stand firmly in your own value set is

2535
01:39:52.945 --> 01:39:54.903
a very attractive quality.

2536
01:39:54.903 --> 01:39:56.213
So, that fear of like,

2537
01:39:56.213 --> 01:39:59.774
"Oh, I'm gonna cause problems in my social circle,"

2538
01:39:59.774 --> 01:40:04.026
a lot of that you'll discover is truly in your imagination.

2539
01:40:04.026 --> 01:40:06.069
Like, I remember when I got sober thinking,

2540
01:40:06.069 --> 01:40:10.737
"Holy shit, I have to go to a wedding in six months

2541
01:40:10.737 --> 01:40:11.945
"and there's a bachelor party.

2542
01:40:11.945 --> 01:40:13.559
"Like, how am I gonna go to that bachelor party

2543
01:40:13.559 --> 01:40:14.642
"and not drink?

2544
01:40:14.642 --> 01:40:16.580
"Like, not only am I gonna be uncomfortable,

2545
01:40:16.580 --> 01:40:18.421
"I'm gonna make everybody else uncomfortable."

2546
01:40:18.421 --> 01:40:20.572
You're future tripping on something

2547
01:40:20.572 --> 01:40:22.312
that hasn't happened yet.

2548
01:40:22.312 --> 01:40:25.957
And when you get there and you kind of walk through it,

2549
01:40:25.957 --> 01:40:27.085
you get to the other side of it,

2550
01:40:27.085 --> 01:40:29.157
and you realize like that just wasn't the big deal

2551
01:40:29.157 --> 01:40:30.176
that I thought it was.

2552
01:40:30.176 --> 01:40:32.722
Like, nobody actually really cares.

2553
01:40:32.722 --> 01:40:34.305
So, value yourself.

2554
01:40:35.295 --> 01:40:38.341
And in that valuing, make those better decisions.

2555
01:40:38.341 --> 01:40:40.896
That self-esteem will begin to flourish and blossom

2556
01:40:40.896 --> 01:40:44.190
and make those healthier choices that align your behavior

2557
01:40:44.190 --> 01:40:45.898
with your values even easier.

2558
01:40:45.898 --> 01:40:47.481
But first you gotta begin.

2559
01:40:47.481 --> 01:40:48.814
So, what is that first step?

2560
01:40:48.814 --> 01:40:51.434
What is the thing you can do right now today

2561
01:40:51.434 --> 01:40:55.492
that will shift that trajectory and start to create momentum

2562
01:40:55.492 --> 01:40:57.917
in the direction that you wanna move?

2563
01:40:57.917 --> 01:40:59.371
That was just so beautifully put.

2564
01:40:59.371 --> 01:41:00.629
I think I didn't realize

2565
01:41:00.629 --> 01:41:05.546
'til just now how much recovery helped you in your approach

2566
01:41:06.796 --> 01:41:10.677
to integrating a plant-based diet and just your wellness.

2567
01:41:10.677 --> 01:41:11.510
Oh, it's huge.

2568
01:41:11.510 --> 01:41:12.915
And like it's so the software.

2569
01:41:12.915 --> 01:41:14.309
Like, I heard all that,

2570
01:41:14.309 --> 01:41:17.139
and I just heard like the recovery software,

2571
01:41:17.139 --> 01:41:19.321
kind of like go into computation mode

2572
01:41:19.321 --> 01:41:22.804
and tackle this issue with this software that works

2573
01:41:22.804 --> 01:41:24.762
and can be applied so many different places.

2574
01:41:24.762 --> 01:41:26.345
It must be such a core element.

2575
01:41:26.345 --> 01:41:28.428
Yeah, it's a rubric for, you know,

2576
01:41:28.428 --> 01:41:31.359
how I make decisions in all facets of my life.

2577
01:41:31.359 --> 01:41:35.098
And certainly, especially when you realize

2578
01:41:35.098 --> 01:41:38.663
how much we eat to kind of salve our emotional states,

2579
01:41:38.663 --> 01:41:41.157
and you realize that there is an addictive nature to that,

2580
01:41:41.157 --> 01:41:45.538
the template of recovery becomes all the more apt.

2581
01:41:45.538 --> 01:41:47.371
And I think it's really instructive

2582
01:41:47.371 --> 01:41:51.012
for any kind of habit change that you're trying to make.

2583
01:41:51.012 --> 01:41:51.970
I love it.

2584
01:41:51.970 --> 01:41:52.928
It was great.

2585
01:41:52.928 --> 01:41:56.636
Can I add just two quick things to that?

2586
01:41:56.636 --> 01:42:00.652
For someone who I'm, as I've said before,

2587
